                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">NSF Certified for Sport</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>

          <p>
            Every product here keeps sugar low, so the real choice comes down to three questions. Do you want dairy or plant protein? Do you want fiber built in, or will you add your own? And how much does independent testing matter to you compared with price? The two NSF certified wheys sit at the premium end; the plant blends are cheaper but deserve a request for recent heavy-metal results. If you also manage type 2 diabetes or prediabetes, our <a href="/best-protein-powder-for-diabetics/">protein powder for diabetics</a> guide covers label reading for blood sugar in more depth.
          </p>
