            One serving a day is usually plenty. Most of your protein should still come from meals such as eggs, fish, chicken, Greek yogurt, tofu, lentils and beans, which also bring fiber, minerals and healthy fats that a shake lacks. If you use a GLP-1 medication for weight or insulin resistance, protein becomes even more important for preserving muscle; our <a href="/best-protein-powder-for-glp-1/">protein powder for GLP-1</a> guide covers that situation.
